{
  "summary": "Backports six pull requests to the 32.x release branch: #36277, #36303, #36340, #36392, #36404, and #36435. The changes include ensuring initial private broadcast connections are fully made and retries are properly tracked, capping the socket wait timeout to fix zero-timeout RPC clients on macOS and BSD systems, improving HTTP receive throttling test logging, and fixing CI/test isolation and fuzzing issues.",
  "problem": "The 32.x branch lacks several fixes already merged on master: private broadcast can fail to complete its intended initial connections or trigger stale retries; running `bitcoin-cli` with `-rpcclienttimeout=0` errors out on macOS because large timeouts cause `select()` to fail with EINVAL; concurrent CI container jobs collide over Docker subnets; and the private broadcast fuzz test fails to explore state due to hardcoded zero-seeding.",
  "evidence": [
    "Commit b2c6f6f027: 'bitcoin-cli turns -rpcclienttimeout=0 into a 5 year timeout and passes it down to Sock::Wait. On systems without poll() (e.g. macOS and the BSDs) the wait is done with select(), which fails with EINVAL for timeouts above 10^8 seconds on macOS... Cap the timeout at INT_MAX milliseconds'",
    "Commit 3c61fa20ef: 'Make sure we send out all three connections when intiating a private broadcast. Use MarkResolved instead of Remove to mark a tx as having been received back or mempool-conflicted. Prevent additional stale retry connections by tracking disconnects and explicitly granting new connections with TryGrantRetry.'"
